Instead of having a single modest step on timeouts at crowning, why not 
let the timeout grow exponentionally?

The first timeout would be something really short like d100 and then 
each time a favor is granted increase it by 10% so it goes d100, d110, 
d121, d133, d146, d160, d176, d193, d212, etc.  So it doubles just over 
each seventh time.

If that doesn't grow fast enough then roll the player's level of dice of 
that size.  So third level and four favors granted would be 3d146.

The result is that prayers work great when the character is just 
starting out then become very very rare near the end.

